Ideally, one should use the ; command very often. I don't believe I've
ever failed to take evasive action from a mumak under the impression it
was a rothe. Though I have on occasion recklessly approached wererats
thinking they were merely the unwere variety.

The colour suggestions fail to take into account the fact that most
people play this on mono screens. Part of the game's charm is the
attractive ascii graphics (I especially enjoy the sanctum sesame
sequence) and I'd hate to see a move toward specialization in fancy
graphics. (Though I often play this on the X interface.)

QMs seems to be sufficiently unique to warrant their own letter. I
wonder about zrutys, though? I think they are only there because ye
devteam couldn't think of anything else to do with the letter z. Maybe
the zombies ought to be split up into small and large? After all, a
gnome zombie is an entirely different kettle of fish from an ettin
zombie.

And a minor flame: mumakil are plural, mumak is singular.
